This is the model for PTMACK for predicting personality, its designed to take specific inputs using this format exactly, x is a floating point number from 0.0 - 10.0.

Any deviation from this input can cause the AI to hallucinate results, its only capable of outputting one of the 3 personalities and will not admit to being wrong, it has been tested extensively on test cases and never failed using this format.

{
"role": "user",

"content": "Predict the personality type:
\nSocial Energy: (x)
\nAlone Time Preference: (x)
\nTalkativeness: (x)
\nDeep Reflection: (x)
\nGroup Comfort: (x)
\nParty Liking: (x)
\nListening Skill: (x)
\nEmpathy: (x)
\nCreativity: (x)
\nOrganization: (x)
\nLeadership: (x)
\nRisk Taking: (x)
\nPublic Speaking Comfort: (x)
\nCuriosity: (x)
\nRoutine Preference: (x)
\nExcitement Seeking: (x)
\nFriendliness: (x)
\nEmotional Stability: (x)
\nPlanning: (x)
\nSpontaneity: (x)
\nAdventurousness: (x)
\nReading Habit: (x)
\nSports Interest: (x)
\nOnline Social Usage: (x)
\nTravel Desire: (x)
\nGadget Usage: (x)
\nWork Style Collaborative: (x)
\nDecision Speed: (x)
\nStress Handling: (x)"
}

You can create the AI on Ollama using the Modelfile and the LLM file like this,

Ollama create {Your chosen name for the local model} -f Modelfile 
---------------------------------------
The model was trained using the cleaned csv that was turned into a json file